# Merseine on a Room made a creature by Opalescence (Glorious Anthem keeps it alive at mana value 0). A Room has the mana
# cost of its unlocked doors alone, and none at all with neither unlocked (CR 709.5). Bot1 casts Unholy Annex, then
# Ephemerate blinks the Room: it returns as a new object with neither door unlocked (CR 709.5d), so with no mana cost, and
# Merseine on it can't be paid for (CR 118.6) even with mana to spare - not a free {0}. Once Bot1 pays {2}{B} to unlock
# Unholy Annex (CR 709.5e), the creature's mana cost is {2}{B}, and that is what removes a net counter: exactly {B}{W}{W}
# in the pool, nothing left. Ephemerate's rebound is declined (the default).
